<title>USA: U.S. Aug business inventories rose 0.5 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Aug business inventories rose 0.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commerce Department said U.S. August business inventories rose 0.5 percent after rising a revised 0.5 percent in July. It said August business sales fell 0.3 percent after a revised 1.0 percent July increase.</p>
<p>The following lists business inventories and sales by</p>
<p>sector, in billions of dollars, seasonally adjusted:</p>
<p>    INVENTORIES:   August	July--Rev from     June</p>
<p> Total Business  1,007.03  1,002.40  1,001.49    997.32</p>
<p> Durable Goods     605.68    601.98    601.14    598.11</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods  401.35    400.42    400.34    399.21</p>
<p>    INVENTORIES:   August	July--Rev from     June</p>
<p> Manufacturers     435.61    434.45    434.52    433.87</p>
<p> Retailers	   311.11    308.86    307.52    304.19</p>
<p> --Auto Dealers     87.83     86.53     86.11</p>
<p> Wholesalers	 260.31    259.10    259.45    259.26</p>
<p>    SALES:	   August	July--Rev from     June</p>
<p> Total Business    717.09    719.18    720.55    711.76</p>
<p> Durable Goods     353.69    354.62    355.67    352.98</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods  363.41    364.56    364.88    358.78</p>
<p>    SALES:	   August	July--Rev from     June</p>
<p> Manufacturers     312.64    312.40    312.67    308.85</p>
<p> Retailers	   204.25    204.72    204.66    204.37</p>
<p> --Auto Dealers     49.98     49.73     49.60</p>
<p> Wholesalers	 200.20    202.06    203.21    198.54</p>
<p> Inventory-To-     August	July--Rev from	June</p>
<p>  Sales Ratio	  1.40	1.39	1.39	1.40</p>
<p>The inventory-to-sales ratio states the number of months it would take to sell existing stocks at the current pace.</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected August business inventories to rise 0.3 percent.  </p>
<p>The department said the August inventory level is the highest ever since it began tracking the data in 1982.</p>
